# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) before building. Analytics config for PostHog.
#
# Vite INLINES `import.meta.env.VITE_*` at build time, so these must exist in
# whatever environment runs `npm run build` — your shell, or the CI/host build
# step. They are NOT runtime config: a Cloudflare secret or a host's runtime
# variable cannot reach an assets-only static deploy, because by then the
# values are already baked into the bundle.
#
# Build without them and `posthog.init()` (src/ui/main.tsx) is handed
# `undefined`. Nothing throws and nothing logs at the user: the site simply
# reports no pageviews, no gameplay events and no crashes, and looks healthy
# while doing it. That is exactly what happened when the site moved from
# Vercel to Cloudflare on 2026-08-15 — the vars lived in the Vercel project
# and were left behind, and production went analytics-dark for five days
# before anyone noticed. To check a deploy:
#
#   curl -s https://worldsoccersim.org/assets/index-*.js | grep -c phc_
#
# Zero means the build was made without a key.
#
# The key below is PostHog's public project API key. It is write-only and is
# already served to every visitor inside the JS bundle, so it is not a secret
# and is checked in deliberately — a placeholder here would leave the next
# person building the same silently-dead bundle.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_nqhYqPRCqWKbvbmWV4Nqs4NzmVP2xA8fUgtAMdGnF9FZ

# Standard PostHog US ingestion endpoint (not the app URL, us.posthog.com).
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
